            "description": "WebSocket endpoints cannot be tested directly in Postman REST requests.\n\n## How to test the WebSocket\n\n**Option 1 — Postman WebSocket Request:**\n1. Click New → WebSocket Request\n2. Enter URL: ws://localhost:8000/api/v1/ws?token={{access_token}}\n3. Connect, then send messages as JSON:\n\n**clipboard_update:**\n```json\n{\n  \"event\": \"clipboard_update\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"content\": \"Hello from WebSocket!\",\n    \"content_type\": \"text\",\n    \"source_device_name\": \"Postman WS Client\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**sync_request:**\n```json\n{\n  \"event\": \"sync_request\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"last_sync_timestamp\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2 — Browser Console:**\n```javascript\nconst ws = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:8000/api/v1/ws?token=YOUR_TOKEN');\nws.onmessage = e => console.log(JSON.parse(e.data));\nws.onopen = () => ws.send(JSON.stringify({\n  event: 'sync_request',\n  data: { last_sync_timestamp: '2026-01-01T00:00:00' }\n}));\n```"
